---A mutation to apply to an entity.
---@class gcp.datastore_v1.Mutation
---@field propertyMask? gcp.datastore_v1.PropertyMask The properties to write in this mutation. None of the properties in the mask may have a reserved name, except for `__key__`. This field is ignored for `delete`. If the entity already exists, only properties referenced in the mask are updated, others are left untouched. Properties referenced in the mask but not in the entity are deleted.
---@field baseVersion? string The version of the entity that this mutation is being applied to. If this does not match the current version on the server, the mutation conflicts.
---@field conflictResolutionStrategy? gcp.datastore_v1.MutationConflictResolutionStrategyEnum|string The strategy to use when a conflict is detected. Defaults to `SERVER_VALUE`. If this is set, then `conflict_detection_strategy` must also be set.
---@field insert? gcp.datastore_v1.Entity The entity to insert. The entity must not already exist. The entity key's final path element may be incomplete.
---@field upsert? gcp.datastore_v1.Entity The entity to upsert. The entity may or may not already exist. The entity key's final path element may be incomplete.
---@field propertyTransforms? gcp.datastore_v1.PropertyTransformList Optional. The transforms to perform on the entity. This field can be set only when the operation is `insert`, `update`, or `upsert`. If present, the transforms are be applied to the entity regardless of the property mask, in order, after the operation.
---@field updateTime? string The update time of the entity that this mutation is being applied to. If this does not match the current update time on the server, the mutation conflicts.
---@field delete? gcp.datastore_v1.Key The key of the entity to delete. The entity may or may not already exist. Must have a complete key path and must not be reserved/read-only.
---@field update? gcp.datastore_v1.Entity The entity to update. The entity must already exist. Must have a complete key path.

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.MutationConflictResolutionStrategyEnum "STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVER_VALUE"|"FAIL"

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.MutationList gcp.datastore_v1.Mutation[]

---The result of applying a mutation.
---@class gcp.datastore_v1.MutationResult
---@field conflictDetected? boolean Whether a conflict was detected for this mutation. Always false when a conflict detection strategy field is not set in the mutation.
---@field transformResults? gcp.datastore_v1.ValueList The results of applying each PropertyTransform, in the same order of the request.
---@field createTime? string The create time of the entity. This field will not be set after a 'delete'.
---@field updateTime? string The update time of the entity on the server after processing the mutation. If the mutation doesn't change anything on the server, then the timestamp will be the update timestamp of the current entity. This field will not be set after a 'delete'.
---@field version? string The version of the entity on the server after processing the mutation. If the mutation doesn't change anything on the server, then the version will be the version of the current entity or, if no entity is present, a version that is strictly greater than the version of any previous entity and less than the version of any possible future entity.
---@field key? gcp.datastore_v1.Key The automatically allocated key. Set only when the mutation allocated a key.

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.MutationResultList gcp.datastore_v1.MutationResult[]

---A partition ID identifies a grouping of entities. The grouping is always by project and namespace, however the namespace ID may be empty. A partition ID contains several dimensions: project ID and namespace ID. Partition dimensions: - May be `""`. - Must be valid UTF-8 bytes. - Must have values that match regex `[A-Za-z\d\.\-_]{1,100}` If the value of any dimension matches regex `__.*__`, the partition is reserved/read-only. A reserved/read-only partition ID is forbidden in certain documented contexts. Foreign partition IDs (in which the project ID does not match the context project ID ) are discouraged. Reads and writes of foreign partition IDs may fail if the project is not in an active state.
---@class gcp.datastore_v1.PartitionId
---@field databaseId? string If not empty, the ID of the database to which the entities belong.
---@field namespaceId? string If not empty, the ID of the namespace to which the entities belong.
---@field projectId? string The ID of the project to which the entities belong.

