---A message that can hold any of the supported value types and associated metadata.
---@class gcp.datastore_v1.Value
---@field blobValue? string A blob value. May have at most 1,000,000 bytes. When `exclude_from_indexes` is false, may have at most 1500 bytes. In JSON requests, must be base64-encoded.
---@field geoPointValue? gcp.datastore_v1.LatLng A geo point value representing a point on the surface of Earth.
---@field doubleValue? number A double value.
---@field integerValue? string An integer value.
---@field nullValue? gcp.datastore_v1.ValueNullValueEnum|string A null value.
---@field booleanValue? boolean A boolean value.
---@field keyValue? gcp.datastore_v1.Key A key value.
---@field entityValue? gcp.datastore_v1.Entity An entity value. - May have no key. - May have a key with an incomplete key path. - May have a reserved/read-only key.
---@field timestampValue? string A timestamp value. When stored in the Datastore, precise only to microseconds; any additional precision is rounded down.
---@field excludeFromIndexes? boolean If the value should be excluded from all indexes including those defined explicitly.
---@field meaning? number The `meaning` field should only be populated for backwards compatibility.
---@field arrayValue? gcp.datastore_v1.ArrayValue An array value. Cannot contain another array value. A `Value` instance that sets field `array_value` must not set fields `meaning` or `exclude_from_indexes`.
---@field stringValue? string A UTF-8 encoded string value. When `exclude_from_indexes` is false (it is indexed) , may have at most 1500 bytes. Otherwise, may be set to at most 1,000,000 bytes.

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.ValueList gcp.datastore_v1.Value[]

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.ValueMap { [string]: gcp.datastore_v1.Value }

---@alias gcp.datastore_v1.ValueNullValueEnum "NULL_VALUE"

